      "figure_captions": [
        "Complete $2^3$ factorial design",
        "Analysis provenance and interpretive roles",
        "Post-primary centered $E\\times L$ exact-gradient contrasts by block count in the original and independent-seed datasets. Points show covariance-aware mixed-model contrasts and bars show unadjusted Wald 95\\% intervals. Shape and line style distinguish datasets; the horizontal reference is zero. The display does not posit a monotonic depth law.",
        "Post-primary H1 weighting summaries. Equal-depth and observation/matched-parameter weighting answer different questions; the adopted pooled estimate is shown separately. Bars are Wald 95\\% intervals, and zero is the reference. Statistical significance is not a criterion for choosing a weighting.",
        "Descriptive multiplicative $E\\times L$ indices conditional on $R=0$. $I_{EL\\mid R=0",
        "Corrected centered H1--H4 family. Decisions follow the primary model-based Wald/Holm rule. Percentile bootstrap intervals corroborate H1; H2 and H3 intervals include zero despite model-based rejection; H4 is unresolved. Fits are completed bootstrap fits, distinct from the 50 independent initialization clusters.",
        "Corrected primary Wald 95\\% intervals and initialization-cluster percentile bootstrap intervals for H1--H4, with a zero reference. H1 used 2,000 completed bootstrap fits; H2--H4 used 443. Marker shape and line style distinguish interval types without reliance on color."
